        "original_id": "01eb61fc-a265-54fa-ad90-859de865249e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: State Theatre, Arts Centre Melbourne, Southbank, Melbourne Arts Precinct, Yarra River, St Kilda Road, Victoria, Australia\n- Organizations: Arts Centre Melbourne\n- Products: Victorian Arts Centre\n- Concepts: performing arts centre, theatres, concert halls\n\nFacts:\n- The State Theatre opened in 1984.\n- The State Theatre is part of Arts Centre Melbourne.\n- The State Theatre is located by the Yarra River and St Kilda Road.\n- Arts Centre Melbourne was originally known as the Victorian Arts Centre.\n- Arts Centre Melbourne was briefly officially called the Arts Centre.\n- Arts Centre Melbourne is a performing arts centre consisting of a complex of theatres and concert halls.\n- Arts Centre Melbourne is in the Melbourne Arts Precinct in Southbank, a central suburb of Melbourne in Victoria, Australia.",
